      "message": "fix(turning): part-off states the piece kept and a back stock\n\nThe Part operation gets one setting, kerf: PartKerf, with two values:\n- kept: the cut-off piece (default, the #3452 kerf on the chuck side)\n  or the chuck piece (the kerf on the free-end side; a stub comes off).\n- back_stock: the whole kerf stands this far off the parting plane,\n  into the scrap side (mm, 0 or more).\n\nThe kernel and the gouge verdict read the scrap side from kept. The\nverdict treats the back stock as part material. A setup that holds the\npart end for end now refuses only the default, and the refusal names\nthe setting. The setting is in the project file (keys written only when\nnot the default), the Passes tab (\"The part is\", \"Back stock\") and MCP\nedit_operation, through EditOperationParams. The stamp folds it only\nwhen not the default, so saved ops do not go stale.\n\nStacked on #3472.\n\nFixes #3469\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
