      "message": "Merge origin/main into issue/3469-part-kept-side\n\nRefresh the part-off kept-piece branch onto main and fix every open\nreview finding.\n\nFindings:\n- Old Part caches: the branch now carries main's #3452 stamp salt\n  (part-off-kerf-side-v1) and the regression test\n  part_off_saved_before_3452.rs. An old centred-kerf cache loads Stale\n  and the post refuses it until the op is generated again.\n- Catalog suite: main's corrected pin (G01 X0. Z12. F0.02) is in the\n  branch. The pin that asked for Z13.5 is gone with the merge.\n- Screenshots: the PR body now links the before and after images from\n  the fork's images-only branch. No image is in this branch.\n- Conflicts: resolved in job.rs, parting_law.rs, turning/mod.rs,\n  lathe_part_off_kerf.rs and setup_align_lathe.rs. Both sides added\n  items in parting_law.rs and turning/mod.rs, so both are kept.\n  #3472 removed reverses_axis, so its precise part_off_problem rule is\n  the flipped-setup refusal. It stays for the default, and the Chuck\n  setting states the side and skips it. The refusal names the setting.\n  The gouge law still judges every path.\n\nIntegration: every OpParams::Part literal in the tests has kerf. The\nmotion and app pins cover the kept piece, the back stock, the flipped\nsetup and the old cache.\n\nRefs #3469\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
